// A second interface definition claiming a name that is already registered used to
// overwrite the first one in silence, so every use of the first interface dispatched
// through the second one's contract (an i32 method read back as an i64, or a bogus
// "does not implement" on a method the class never declared). Two interfaces named
// the same in DIFFERENT namespaces are fine - each registers as "ns.IFace" - but a
// redefinition within one scope is now rejected.
expect_error("interface 'IDupIface' is already defined at")
{
    interface IDupIface { int a(); };
    interface IDupIface { i64 b(); };
}

// The def-site key used to be a bare basename ("file(line,col)" from GetSourceFileName()), so
// two files sharing a basename could collide invisibly whenever their definitions also landed
// on the same line and column. iface_defsite_helper/err_duplicate_interface_name.cb below
// shares THIS file's basename on purpose and is padded so its "interface IFooDefsite" lands on
// the exact same line/col as the one in the block below - reproducing the pre-fix hole (old key
// would compare equal: same basename, same line, same col, stayed silent). The fixed key uses
// the canonical full path, so the two files now compare unequal and the guard fires here, during
// this file's own body walk (not an import-time abort, so it coexists with the IDupIface case
// above).
//
// The expect_error text below pins the helper's exact reported basename+(line,col) tail:
// "err_duplicate_interface_name.cb(41,4)". On the FIXED compiler the guard fires regardless of
// whether the two files' line/col still coincide - full path identity does not care - so this
// pinned tail is not load-bearing for pass/fail today. It exists as a tripwire: if the padding
// below (or the helper's own padding, see that file's line 41) ever drifts apart, this
// exact-location match breaks and the test fails LOUDLY (mismatched expect_error text) instead
// of quietly stopping to exercise the historical same-line/col coincidence that made this
// regression reproducible pre-fix. THIS LINE MUST STAY AT LINE 41, COLUMN 4 (four-space indent)
// to keep matching the helper file's line 41. The pin deliberately starts AFTER the directory
// portion (Test/library/iface_defsite_helper/), not at "already defined at": expect_error does
// a plain substring find(), and ShortenDefSiteForDisplay renders that directory with NATIVE path
// separators (forward slash here, backslash on Windows) - a substring spanning "at" through the
// directory into the basename would never match on one platform or the other. Anchoring on the
// basename+(line,col)+trailing-clause tail alone stays a true substring on both.
import "iface_defsite_helper/err_duplicate_interface_name.cb";

expect_error("err_duplicate_interface_name.cb(41,4) - an interface name must be unique within its namespace")
{
    interface IFooDefsite { i64 b(); };
}

extern int main()
{
    return 0;
}
